p>| Update any stale statuses flagged and ensure workflows are current | CRM / workflow hygiene | Adviser (Paul) | 2026-03-18 | Reporting inaccuracies; missed tasks; cases drifting |</p><p>---</p><p>## Email Recap (auto-generated from review)</p><p>**Subject:** Weekly Performance Review and Agreed Actions</p><p>Hi Paul,</p><p>Below is a summary of this week’s review and agreed actions.</p><p>### Follow-Up From Last Week</p><p>**Completed actions**</p><p>- Reduced overdue workflow items from **~20** to **12** currently.</p><p>- **Brianna Kennedy:** **EWS1** resolved; **NatWest application submitted** (CRM/report update expected to reflect on the next report run).</p><p>- **Raymond:** documents received; moved back into today for progression.</p><p>**Outstanding actions (with owner and revised deadline)**</p><p>- Clear or re-task **12 overdue** workflow items (oldest due **2026-03-05**, **6 days overdue** as of **2026-03-11**) — **Owner: Paul** — **Deadline: 2026-03-12**.</p><p>- Correct any remaining staging/ownership issues (including at least **1** lead from last week needing correction) — **Owner: Paul** — **Deadline: 2026-03-12**.</p><p>### Performance Snapshot (sections discussed)</p><p>**Key figures**</p><p>- **Appointments/leads:** **10** last week; **4** held so far this week (**3 on 2026-03-09**, **1 on 2026-03-10**) despite one reporting view showing **0**.</p><p>- **Written business (March):** **£6k** so far; February written referenced as **£16.4k**.</p><p>- **Banked income (February):** just shy of **£13k**.</p><p>- **Projected income discussed:** **~£40k** in view (approx **£12k banked + £22k April + just over £6k March still to come**).</p><p>- **Pipeline volume:** **13** mortgage applications currently + **7** to add (**20** total); **4** insurance cases.</p><p>**What is working**</p><p>- Mortgage momentum is building and translating into written/banked performance visibility.</p><p>- Overdue workflow count reduced materially vs last week.</p><p>- Good handover on Karen’s returning client (DIP produced; notes sent to **Karen and Megan**).</p><p>**Identified risks**</p><p>- **CRM discipline/SLA risk:** **12** overdues; oldest follow-ups due **2026-03-05** remain incomplete by **2026-03-11**.</p><p>- **Reporting inconsistency:** appointments held vs “0 this week” view.</p><p>- **Protection conversion risk:** **4** insurance cases vs mortgage pipeline moving towards **20**; weak visibility after first protection appointment.</p><p>- **Compliance/admin risk:** submitted remortgage (proc fee **~£5,400–£5,500**) still needs notes/report.</p><p>### Cases Requiring Attention (client name, issue, owner)</p><p>- **Steph Mitchell:** product transfer stalled/overdue follow-up — **Owner: Paul**.</p><p>- **Graham Braid:** remortgage docs received; progress to submission — **Owner: Paul**.</p><p>- **Jacob Juarez:** remortgage docs received; needs booking — **Owner: Paul**.</p><p>- **Lloyd Dunlop:** docs received; needs booking (stalled at depth) — **Owner: Paul**.</p><p>- **Raymond:** remortgage docs received; progress now — **Owner: Paul**.</p><p>- **Mendon:** purchase (~£600k), offer accepted; document next steps after appointment — **Owner: Paul**.</p><p>- **Edinburgh referral via Gavin:** purchase (~£1m), docs received; booking required — **Owner: Paul**.</p><p>- **Angie Ray:** B&amp;C referral not yet made to Megan; protection review scheduled **2026-03-13** — **Owner: Paul + Megan**.</p><p>- **Paul Clarkson:** protection progress stalling due to non-response; triage/escalate chase if needed — **Owner: Paul (triage), Sean (if escalated)**.</p><p>- **Jamie Braithwaite:** push to provider/application stage; health questions required (completion referenced mid April) — **Owner: Paul then Sean**.</p><p>- **Wendy Watson:** progress to application; health questions required; priority on risk ASAP — **Owner: Paul then Sean**.</p><p>### Revenue and Pipeline Risks (discussed)</p><p>- Pipeline banking is vulnerable to slippage if a