at you on this one, But we do need to try to make sure that this gets cleared pretty much daily. You know, twenty down to six is a huge result, But we need to try to make sure that you try to pretty much clear it or your overdues are one or two days, because six days is I would say probably too excessive for somebody that you&#x27;ve said that you might be phoning back a week ago since yeah, they&#x27;re checking in. So I would certainly say, you know have a, Decision every day, you know, Is that going to be a new job? Or is that going to be a Sean job? Is what I would say. Yeah, because Sean can phone somebody quickly in thirty seconds, update the workflow, fire them out an email copy you into and then re- derise it. You know for a week down the line. Yeah yeah, whereas if you are trying to bash out report Sean, you wouldn&#x27;t mind picking up a thirty second call. Would you?</p><p>Sean McLennan: No problem at all no.</p><p>Bob Duncan: So just kind of have a bit of uh, A kind of a mindset of, am I actually going to do these today? You know, if the mindset is I&#x27;m going to do them, great. But then if you get to three o&#x27;clock in the afternoon and you&#x27;re like, actually I&#x27;ve got seven applications, seven reports to start working through. Are you realistically going to do them? Probably not. Yeah. So have about an honesty session with yourself and ask for the support from Sean to chase up things like that. Yeah. Okay okay.</p><p>Bob Duncan: Let&#x27;s have a look at leads and opportunities, etc. So, leads last week for you. I&#x27;ll just share my screen in a second, Paul. Just want to get it up. So I think quite encouragingly at the moment is I know you are definitely feeling busier, which is really good. And I know we did talk about it last week because I threw in a couple of extra appointments, which frustrated you. And. But that&#x27;s okay. You&#x27;re allowed to be frustrated, but I think ten new appointments last week, which I think is really